# L §4.2: a calendar's added window "is one the line meets, so a result that depends on its day is HOLE-IMPRECISE
# unless the line states windows each (§4.4)" (L4_2_added_window.test). L §4.4: "That holds for every
# window, wherever the line meets it: ... a day in a calendar's added list (§4.2)"; windows each splits the line per
# sub-window. len adds a day in window(2026-03-02, 2026-03-04): 03-03 is no business day only where the added day is
# 03-03 (q3); len2's one_of([03-10, 03-12]): 03-10 is no business day only where the added day is 03-10 (q4).
# (Writer 8: windows earliest and latest are gone, q1 and q2 with them.) The each label is this interpreter's. (Writer 6's reading, "§8.1 only", reversed: round 14's U-6.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input len: calendar
input len2: calendar

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026
  known 2025-12-01
  len = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], added [window(2026-03-02, 2026-03-04)])
  len2 = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], added [one_of([2026-03-10, 2026-03-12])])

ask q3: is_business(2026-03-03, len) windows each
ask q4: is_business(2026-03-10, len2) windows each
=== expect
q3 [added window(2026-03-02, 2026-03-04) = 2026-03-02]: true
  cut 2026-12-31
q3 [added window(2026-03-02, 2026-03-04) = 2026-03-03]: false
  cut 2026-12-31
q3 [added window(2026-03-02, 2026-03-04) = 2026-03-04]: true
  cut 2026-12-31
q4 [added one_of([2026-03-10, 2026-03-12]) = 2026-03-10]: false
  cut 2026-12-31
q4 [added one_of([2026-03-10, 2026-03-12]) = 2026-03-12]: true
  cut 2026-12-31
